---
import '../styles/orientation-landing.css';
import '../styles/atlas-lexicon.css';
import HearthNavigation from './HearthNavigation.astro';
const families = [
  { number:'I', title:'Keep the sourcechain visible', note:'Terms that keep language answerable to what is known.', terms:[['Source','The closest authoritative material a statement depends on.','3,658'],['Evidence','A checkable observation that supports but does not decide.','2,884'],['Claim','A statement whose scope, maturity, and limit can be inspected.','692'],['Boundary','The line beyond which a task, claim, or capability must not silently travel.','968']]},
  { number:'II', title:'Prepare the working bench', note:'Named information objects passed between people, agents, and tools.', terms:[['Artifact','A durable output with an owner, location, state, and review route.','707'],['Packet','A bounded bundle selected for a particular reader or task.','1,057'],['Schema','A typed contract for record shape and required relations.','771'],['Receipt','A time-bounded account of inputs, checks, results, and non-implications.','1,662']]},
  { number:'III', title:'Bank the returnthread', note:'Terms that describe controlled transitions and continuation.', terms:[['Route','A resolved path from present state to an allowed destination.','1,400'],['Projection','A derived view that remains answerable to its source.','1,140'],['Handoff','The exact state, evidence, and next action transferred to another actor.','536'],['Return','The preserved way to re-enter, correct, or continue work.','1,516']]},
  { number:'IV', title:'Keep the decision human-held', note:'Terms that prevent automation from becoming silent authority.', terms:[['Authority','The established right to decide or cause a particular effect.','2,592'],['Owner','The person or role accountable for a path, artifact, or decision.','1,309'],['Human gate','A consequential choice explicitly returned to a person.','924 human'],['Release','A separately authorized transition, never implied by a successful check.','991']]}
] as const;
const roadmap = [
  ['01','Orient',['Name the decision','Select direct sources','Choose one context profile','State the stop condition']],
  ['02','Bound',['Create a task envelope','Declare authority and tools','Name owned and no-touch paths','Define evidence and handoff']],
  ['03','Work',['Use ReAct for tool loops','Use structured reasoning for decomposition','Use independent workers for alternatives','Use a critic for counterevidence']],
  ['04','Return',['Validate the artifact','Preserve a receipt','Surface uncertainty and nonclaims','Hand the decision to its owner']]
] as const;
---
<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="UTF-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"/><meta name="description" content="A connected vocabulary and roadmap for Hearth & Code methods, agentic engineering, and human-held work."/><meta name="theme-color" content="#1c1714"/><title>Atlas | Hearth &amp; Code</title></head><body class="orientation-body"><div class="orientation-atmosphere" aria-hidden="true"></div><a class="orientation-skip" href="#main-content">Skip to content</a><HearthNavigation current="atlas" context="Atlas / connected language and working routes" /><main id="main-content"><section class="builder-hero"><p class="orientation-kicker">Agentic engineering lexicon / roadmap</p><h1>The Atlas maps the language that moves the work.</h1><p class="orientation-lede">The Library defines techniques. The Atlas shows the vocabulary and sequence that connect them: how a question becomes an artifact, how an agent acts inside a boundary, and how the result returns to human judgment.</p></section><section class="atlas-method"><div><p class="orientation-kicker">Language evidence</p><h2>A practical lexicon derived from recurring use.</h2></div><div><p>This projection uses an aggregate lexical scan of authorized Hub goal prompts, project-resumption records, and Ember Circuit working material. Counts describe occurrences in that bounded corpus, not importance or universal terminology. Raw sessions and private prompt bodies are not reproduced.</p><p>The terms were selected by frequency plus operational distinctiveness, then grouped by the job they perform.</p></div></section><section class="atlas-families">{families.map(family => <article><header><span>{family.number}</span><div><h2>{family.title}</h2><p>{family.note}</p></div></header><dl>{family.terms.map(([term,definition,count]) => <div><dt>{term}<small>{count}</small></dt><dd>{definition}</dd></div>)}</dl></article>)}</section><section class="atlas-roadmap" aria-labelledby="roadmap-title"><div class="orientation-section-heading"><p class="orientation-kicker">A Hearth &amp; Code roadmap</p><h2 id="roadmap-title">Four stages, four practices each.</h2><p>The roadmap composes familiar agentic patterns with the operational-intelligence boundary: reasoning and tool use remain useful only while sources, authority, evidence, and return stay visible.</p></div><ol>{roadmap.map(([number,title,steps]) => <li><span>{number}</span><h3>{title}</h3><ul>{steps.map(step => <li>{step}</li>)}</ul></li>)}</ol></section><section class="atlas-crosswalk"><p class="orientation-kicker">Technique crosswalk</p><div><article><h2>Structured reasoning</h2><p>Use stepwise decomposition or branching search when a task genuinely requires intermediate state. Preserve the decision-relevant summary and checks; do not confuse a fluent reasoning trace with faithful evidence.</p></article><article><h2>ReAct</h2><p>Interleave reasoning, one authorized action, and direct observation. Update the hypothesis after each tool result and stop when the task becomes decision-ready or reaches a boundary.</p></article><article><h2>Mixture of agents</h2><p>Use independent workers when they create distinct evidence or approaches. Add a critic for counterexamples and a human judge for consequential selection. More agents without role separation create repetition.</p></article><article><h2>Chain of verification</h2><p>Verify source fidelity, execution, artifact behavior, adversarial failure, and human meaning as separate layers. Each check proves only its own claim.</p></article></div></section></main><footer class="orientation-footer"><p>Hearth &amp; Code</p><a href="/method/">Continue to Methods →</a></footer></body></html>
